Certainly! The MLST command is typically used to retrieve information about a specific file or directory, while the ABOR command is used to abort a command in progress. Here is the modified sequence of client requests with the MLST and ABOR commands added in appropriate locations:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
MLST test  # Added to retrieve information about the newly created directory 'test'
MKD test
ABOR  # Added to abort any ongoing command if necessary
QUIT
```

In this sequence, the MLST command is placed after the LIST command to get details about the 'test' directory that was just created. The ABOR command is included after the MKD command to demonstrate its usage, although it may not be strictly necessary in this context

